# Binary assets: never line-ending converted.
#
# Git guesses text vs binary from NUL bytes in the first 8 KB. A small,
# generated PDF can have none, so autocrlf rewrites its newlines on checkout and
# the xref offsets no longer match — a label that opens on the machine that
# committed it and is corrupt everywhere else. The STL and 3mf files are only
# safe today because the heuristic happens to get them right.
*.pdf   binary
*.stl   binary
*.3mf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.bin   binary
*.der   binary
